    "guardrails": "This business is a referral/advertising network, not the crew performing the work — never write \"our team\" doing the repair/removal/restoration itself, never claim to directly perform, install, extract, remove, or repair anything, and never claim to employ technicians. Never use the words \"vetted\", \"screened\", \"background-checked\", \"certified\", \"licensed\", or \"accredited\" to describe the providers in the network — even softened or implied — unless that is explicitly given as a fact. Describe the connection itself (fast, local, responsive), not an unverified quality-control process. Always frame the work as done by the independent local providers this business connects customers to. Never claim to be factory authorized, manufacturer certified, or an approved warranty servicer. Do not quote prices, call-out fees, or parts availability. Do not promise same-day or next-day service as a guarantee — describe it as often available, never certain. Do not name a brand as serviced unless it appears in the site's own brand pages. Never state how long a repair will take or how long a part will last.",
